rner H1 using the diagonal (H1-G2-F3, since F3 becomes `@` after your move).\n    -   Furthermore, by flipping the diagonal F3-E4-D5 to `@`, you prevent the opponent from using that diagonal to access H1 themselves.\n    -   **Verdict**: Best Move.\n\nEvaluation: (G, 2) is the best strategic option as it avoids giving away corners directly (unlike A2 and H2) and sets up a tactical sequence to potentially capture the H1 corner, whereas B2 provides the opponent with safe edge moves.\n\nReason: Moves (A, 2) and (H, 2) are blunders that immediately surrender the corners A1 and H1 to the opponent. (B, 2) flips too many discs and allows the opponent to solidify the top-left edge. (G, 2) is a calculated move that sets a trap: if the opponent attacks the exposed piece, it enables you to capture the H1 corner on the next turn.\n\nAnswer: (G, 2)'}
